<title>ARGENTINA: Tax revenue breakdown in Argentine '97 budget bill.</title>
<headline>Tax revenue breakdown in Argentine '97 budget bill.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's 1997 budget bill foresees a 15.8 percent rise in public sector revenue and 15.2 percent for the national administration, as broken down in the following table:</p>
<p> Tax type:	Public sector:     National administration:</p>
<p> Income		+24.2 pct	    +18.6</p>
<p> VAT		   + 6.5 pct	     +3.4 pct</p>
<p> Internal	     -0.1 pct	     +8.6</p>
<p> Foreign trade     +23.3		  +23.3</p>
<p> Fuel		  +77.3		  +77.3</p>
<p> Personal wealth   +13.1		  -37.1</p>
<p> Other		 +10.1		  +12.9</p>
<p>-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0695</p>
</text>
